# The trained checkpoint. ~1.1 GB, with a single 1068 MB file inside it.
#
# GitHub rejects any file over 100 MB in regular git, so this CANNOT be
# committed here — the push would fail outright. It ships as a GitHub Release
# asset instead (2 GB limit, free), fetched by:
#
#     python serving/get_model.py
#
# Excluded rather than left to chance: `git add -A` would otherwise stage a
# gigabyte and fail confusingly halfway through.
serving/model/
serving/*.zip

# Credentials. NEVER commit these — this repo is deployed as a static site,
# so anything tracked here is downloadable from the public URL.
#
# js/mcp_config.json held a Supabase personal access token (sbp_...) and was
# committed in c206e71. It has been removed from the working tree, but it is
# still in git history, so that token must be REVOKED, not just deleted:
#   Supabase > Account > Access Tokens
js/mcp_config.json
**/mcp_config.json
.env
.env.*

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
